From e6a5224fb637a12b7775135a24bb472e473d9234 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 15:10:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: remove manual language switch, follow browser language
 only
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Per explicit request: the EN/IT toggle (top-right on every public
page) let visitors override the detected language. Removed entirely —
LanguageSwitcher.tsx deleted, no longer rendered in layout.tsx.

LocaleSync now keeps the locale cookie continuously in sync with the
browser's navigator.language instead of only writing it once and then
freezing it (the old comment literally said it was preserving "a
manual choice made via the LanguageSwitcher"). With the switch gone,
that freeze served no purpose and meant a visitor who changed their
OS/browser language later would stay stuck on whatever locale their
first visit detected. Now it re-checks on every mount and rewrites the
cookie whenever it disagrees with the current navigator.language — the
only way to change the site's language is to change the browser's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XBj5YyCv7itzLP8BDyrEj5
